Using a dual 8x8 pair-list setup updated with dynamic, rolling pruning:
  outer list: updated every 100 steps, buffer 0.154 nm, rlist 1.154 nm
  inner list: updated every  12 steps, buffer 0.005 nm, rlist 1.005 nm
At tolerance 0.005 kJ/mol/ps per atom, equivalent classical 1x1 list would be:
  outer list: updated every 100 steps, buffer 0.304 nm, rlist 1.304 nm
  inner list: updated every  12 steps, buffer 0.053 nm, rlist 1.053 nm

The non-bonded pair calculation algorithm tolerates a few missing pair interactions close to the cut-off. This can lead to a systematic overestimation of the pressure due to missing LJ interactions. The error in the average pressure due to missing LJ interactions is at most 0.56 bar.
The pressure error can be controlled by setting the environment variable GMX_VERLET_BUFFER_PRESSURE_TOLERANCE to the allowed error in units of bar.

Using Lorentz-Berthelot Lennard-Jones combination rule

NOTE: The number of threads is not equal to the number of (logical) cpus
      and the -pin option is set to auto: will not pin threads to cpus.
      This can lead to significant performance degradation.
